most of america's lifting coveted  restrictions one of the world's biggest  cities has been shut down shanghai home  to about 25 million people is largely at  a standstill today as china battles its  worst wave of covet infections since the  start of this global pandemic in 2020  lucy kraft explains how this lockdown  has raised questions about china's  so-called zero-covid strategy  shanghai's lockdown was supposed to last  just a few days rolled out in stages to  minimize disruption but that plan has  been abandoned and now most of shanghai  china's largest and wealthiest city has  been shut down with no telling when life  could get back to normal  shanghai's modern streets have been  transformed into a post-apocalyptic  landscape  residents have been barricaded into  their homes allowed out only for covid  testing even infants are being screened  residents aren't allowed to walk their  dogs the only canines permitted on city  streets are robots broadcasting  anti-infection tips  frustration is so widespread over panic  buying and persistent food shortages it  inspired a rap song  [Music]  american sean ryan lives in shanghai is  there any sense at all that this is  overkill that the zero covet strategy  maybe has worn out its usefulness that  there should be a more flexible approach  i think there are a lot of people in  shanghai who are saying you know right  now the medicine is worse than the  disease we have people who are dying  because they can't get access to medical  care how many people have actually died  from this recent surge of kovid and the  government has told us zero  it's unclear how long shanghai's mass  lockdown will last residents are bracing  for possibly weeks of home confinement  but despite the strain on residents  china vows it will maintain its zero  covenant policy  lucy kraft cbs mornings tokyo
 

